Now code structure:

- Precompute for each nums[i] the set of (v, min_ops) where v <= sum, min_ops is minimal ops to reach v from nums[i]
- DP array size sum+1, dp[0]=0, others inf
- For each nums[i], new_dp = [inf]*(sum+1)
  - For s in 0..sum:
    - For each (v,d) in pairs[i]:
      - not include: if new_dp[s] > dp[s] + d, set new_dp[s] = dp[s] + d
      - include: if s >= v and new_dp[s+v] > dp[s] + d, set new_dp[s+v] = dp[s] + d
  - dp = new_dp
- Answer = dp[sum] if dp[sum] < inf else -1

But not include: for each (v,d), we can choose not include and pay d, so for all s, new_dp[s] = min(new_dp[s], dp[s] + d)

Include: for each (v,d), new_dp[s+v] = min(new_dp[s+v], dp[s] + d) for s+v<=sum

